<!-- Content-Security-Policy as a <meta> element, because GitHub Pages serves
     static files and cannot set response headers. A meta CSP is genuinely
     weaker than the header: `frame-ancestors`, `report-uri` and `sandbox` are
     IGNORED in meta form (W3C CSP3 §3.3), and it applies only once the parser
     reaches it. It still stops an injected external script and an exfiltrating
     `connect-src`, which is the realistic risk for a static docs site.
     `unsafe-inline` is required on both script-src and style-src: mdBook emits
     inline theme and sidebar scripts and inline styles of its own. -->
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'">
<meta name="referrer" content="strict-origin-when-cross-origin">
